From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iceland <iceland@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:51:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/30] simplefb: iceland gvm: --simplefb software display in
 host-shared memory (after DroidVM)

crosvm run --simplefb width=W,height=H[,format=a8r8g8b8|x8r8g8b8][,poll-hz=N]
(aarch64; default format a8r8g8b8 as DroidVM, poll-hz 60):

- the framebuffer is its own guest-memory region (purpose SharedFramebuffer)
  just below the static swiotlb at the top of the --mem block, 2 MiB
  aligned; Gunyah SHARES it like the swiotlb (set_user_memory_region + an
  shm vdevice node, never lent), so the host reads it while a protected
  guest draws;
- the guest gets a no-map reserved-memory region and a simple-framebuffer
  node (reg, width, height, stride, format, memory-region) for simpledrm;
- a bridge thread opens a window through the gpu_display Wayland backend
  (--wayland-sock, title / app id / decoration / GVM-WINDOW-CLOSE as for the
  virtio-gpu window), polls the framebuffer at poll-hz (dcache invalidated
  before each read), presents it only when the bytes changed, and routes the
  window's keyboard and touch (left button) into a virtio-input keyboard
  and multi-touch device;
- logs GVM-SIMPLEFB WxH format stride base size at start and
  GVM-SIMPLEFB-FRAME n t= mean= nonzero= every 10 s for the first minute,
  then every minute.

Works with or without --gpu; the virtio-gpu window is unchanged.
Design and the cache invalidation ported from DroidVM dvm-crosvm 849e05f
(GPL-2.0-or-later): aarch64/src/simplefb.rs and
src/crosvm/sys/linux/simplefb_display.rs keep DroidVM's header; see CREDITS,
LICENSE.GPL-2.0, ADDITIONAL-PERMISSIONS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
